   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Three classes, not three pronunciations",
     "texto": [
      "There are 44 traditional consonant letters; two are almost obsolete. To read modern words, it helps to recognise the other 42. They are grouped into **mid class**, **high class** and **low class**. The class does not tell you on its own how to pronounce the consonant: it helps you work out the tone of the syllable."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Letters and sounds",
     "texto": [
      "Several letters can represent the same starting sound. For example, **ข** and **ค** both start with a sound like «k», but they belong to different classes, so they can produce different tones. Learn each letter together with its class; do not try to work it out from the sound alone."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
